OL,3,ADolly Parton: Life of the music legend
OL,4,Awhose songs touched millions
OL,5,
OL,6,FDolly Parton, the country singer from
OL,7,Fthe Smoky Mountains of Tennessee, will
OL,8,Fbe remembered for her songs that told
OL,9,Fbeautiful stories so honestly, such as
OL,10,FCoat of Many Colors, Jolene and I Will
OL,11,FAlways Love You.
OL,13,FIn a seven-decade career, Parton won 10
OL,14,FGrammy awards, sold more than 100
OL,15,Fmillion records worldwide, and wrote in
OL,16,Fexcess of 3,000 songs.
OL,18,FParton took her writing seriously, and
OL,19,Fconsidered herself a songwriter over
OL,20,Feverything else. "It's my way of
OL,21,Fexpressing myself," she said. "It's my
OL,22,Ftherapy."
OL,23,APub: 25-AugQpppppppppppppppppppppG12/18
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
FL,163,160,200,105,0,100
PN,11913
SC,0013
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1787703534
OL,1,W5j 5Q7+j 55"k#j 5w;js1
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-.*,%-,* *,%%**,$ ,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,ADolly Parton: Life of the music legend
OL,4,Awhose songs touched millions
OL,5,
OL,6,FShe was also a savvy businesswoman who
OL,7,Fwasn't afraid to make tough decisions.
OL,8,FArmed with a quick wit and southern
OL,9,Fcharm, she took control of her
OL,10,Fshowbusiness career that spanned more
OL,11,Fthan 60 years.
OL,23,APub: 25-AugQpppppppppppppppppppppG13/18
